<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    The hospital tab: every patient the colony has, sorted into what you would do about each one.

    order 41 puts it immediately after our animals tab (40), so the two census screens that answer
    "who is in trouble" sit together in the bar.

    No defaultHotKey. Vanilla has no hospital tab and therefore no key a player already presses for
    one, and inventing a binding is a conflict somebody has to go and resolve for no gain.

    Colony Hospital's own tab is suppressed in UIButtonBarConfig.Suppressed and redirected here by
    Patch_MainTabsRoot_ToggleTab_Hospital, but only when that mod is loaded and this def exists.
    With neither hospital mod installed nothing is suppressed and nothing is redirected.

    validWithoutMap is false: every row is read off a map's pawns, so there is nothing to show from
    the world view.
  -->
  <MainButtonDef>
    <defName>Gideon_Hospital</defName>
    <label>hospital</label>
    <description>Every patient the colony has, in the order you would treat them: who is critical, who is being treated and how it is going, who is waiting on a surgeon, and who is simply getting better. Operations are queued from a two pane picker that shows the surgeon and the odds before you commit, and standing orders deliver medication on a schedule with a nurse's name against them.</description>
    <tabWindowClass>Gideon.UIOverhaul.Features.Hospital.MainTabWindow_Hospital</tabWindowClass>
    <validWithoutMap>false</validWithoutMap>
    <closesWorldView>true</closesWorldView>

    <!--
      No file extension and no Textures prefix: RimWorld's ContentFinder takes a path relative to
      Textures and appends the extension itself. The existing Medical icon, which is already in the
      same flat grayscale as the rest of this mod's main button icons and so tints with the palette.
    -->
    <iconPath>UI/MainButtonIcons/Medical</iconPath>

    <order>41</order>
  </MainButtonDef>

</Defs>
